   "evidence": "In `Bimodule.lean` the grep finds only `pathChain_isDGBimodule` (line 49) and `noncomputable abbrev pathChainBimodule` (line 58). It has no lemma about its differential or grading. `Concatenation.lean:229` holds `private theorem pathChainBimodule_differential ... := (rfl)`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicTopology/DGLocalSystem/Path/Concatenation.lean",
   "fix": "Move it to `DGLocalSystem/Path/Bimodule.lean` as a public `theorem pathChainBimodule_differential ... := (rfl)`, possibly `@[simp]`. Add a public lemma there saying `cubicalChainModuleLof _ _ R p x \u2208 (pathChainBimodule B a b R).grading p`, and derive `pathPointChain_mem` from it.",
   "issue": "`pathChainBimodule_differential` (the differential of `pathChainBimodule B a b R` is `cubicalChainModuleDifferential`) restates how a public definition is built, with no tie to this proof, yet it is `private` here. Every later user of the path bimodule's differential (the basepoint-change transfer to DG local systems) would have to restate it. The same applies to the grading fact behind `pathPointChain_mem`: `(pathChainBimodule B a b R).grading p` is the cubical grading, so `cubicalChainModuleLof_mem` lands in it.",
   "line": 229
  }
 ],
